    "introduction": "Rio Tinto extracts and processes minerals used in construction, manufacturing, transport and energy infrastructure. Its portfolio includes iron ore, aluminium, copper and lithium, supported by mines, processing plants, transport facilities and other industrial assets. Customers buy materials whose prices are largely determined in international commodity markets. Revenue therefore reflects both production volumes and market prices, while profitability depends on resource quality, extraction costs and efficient logistics. Developing or expanding a mine requires major investment and long planning periods. The group also manages environmental obligations and relationships with host communities, with access to energy, water and infrastructure affecting the economics of individual operations.",
